#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1011 expect=violation domain=TD
#note "The rule's variable list also names the four TD trial-design interval variables by their full name. TDTGTPAI='2 weeks' on row 1 is not an ISO 8601 duration; TDSTOFF/TDMINPAI/TDMAXPAI are valid. Pins the four FULL-NAME (non---prefixed) alternatives in the regex. Sheet-safe under SD0003-F1: SD1011's own sheet cell names TRIAL DESIGN minus TA/TI/TS/TV, i.e. TD is IN scope under the sheet reading as well as under the shipped [ALL]. ADAPTED-FROM fda/FDA-SD1011/FDA-SD1011-invalid_td-TD.cdt (verbatim)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset TD class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Disease Assessments"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TDORDER  type=Num  label="Order of Assessment Schedule"
col TDANCVAR type=Char label="Anchor Variable Name"
col TDSTOFF  type=Char label="Offset from the Anchor"
col TDTGTPAI type=Char label="Planned Assessment Interval"
col TDMINPAI type=Char label="Planned Assessment Interval Minimum"
col TDMAXPAI type=Char label="Planned Assessment Interval Maximum"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TD | 1 | RSSTDTC | P0D | 2 weeks | P12D | P16D
